  "label": "Leakage Aware Model Evaluation",
  "related": [
    "protein-generation-b3ca",
    "conformational-protein-8241",
    "cellular-electron-economy-e434"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "optimal-transport-flow-matching-ea35",
  "summary": "New benchmarks, conformal FDR control and negative post-training results show dataset properties and splits, not architecture, often govern reported performance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is stricter evaluation of molecular and protein predictors rather than new architectures. Protify standardizes protein language model benchmarking across zero-shot, supervised and transfer settings and reports task dependence and homology leakage. A OneProt profiling study of allosteric versus orthosteric site classification finds that dataset properties dominate performance over encoder choice. PeptSol contributes 1388 curated protected-peptide solubility measurements with chemistry-aware splits for evaluating seven frozen molecular encoders. PPI-Caliper applies conformal calibration to protein language model interaction scores, controlling false discovery rate without retraining across five species. A fixed-budget DiffDock post-training study reports that focused or mixed torsional supervision gave no improvement over broad score-field continuation. Other work targets generalization directly: FedSPL addresses scaffold heterogeneity in federated property prediction, and contrastive learning improves VOC–olfactory receptor binding prediction on M2OR and iOBPdb. What is new is the treatment of split design, leakage control, formal error control and negative results as central to judging model claims.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
